<title>USA: PAGES CFO resigns, names interim CFO.</title>
<headline>PAGES CFO resigns, names interim CFO.</headline>
<dateline>ST. PETERSBURG, Fla. 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>PAGES Inc said on Wednesday its chief financial officer, Tamara Zeph, had resigned to accept a position at another company and Randall Asmo, the vice president, was named interim CFO and treasurer.</p>
<p>Amos had been with the company since 1990 and had held financial positions with increasing responsibility, the company said.</p>
<p>PAGES creates, publishes and sells books and curriculum-related materials to schools, libraries and schoolchildren in the United States.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
